kubeos-control-plane (1.37.2-1kubeos2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ship the unit enablement as a package file. Build hook 9050 called
    systemctl enable for these units, which a package must not do: it aborts a
    chroot build (the trap documented in that hook). A .wants symlink owned by
    dpkg is the same declaration, so a node installed from the archive alone
    comes up identically.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0530

kubeos-control-plane (1.37.2-1kubeos1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: kube-apiserver, kube-controller-manager, kube-scheduler and
    kube-proxy at v1.37.2 (the version the kubelet package carries) plus etcd and
    etcdctl at the tag kubeadm pins, with their five units and the Apache-2.0 notices
    build hook 9025 used to install into /usr/local/bin.

